{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Measurement (read-only, local tickets store at 0cfe41cb779, which matches origin/tickets; review-bot REVIEW_RESULT sidecars on code_review artifact tickets, so no SSM read was needed).\n\nMethod: scanned every `*-REVIEW_RESULT.json` whose payload schema is `code_review_result_v1`/`_v2` (3,690 of 9,769 sidecars; 3,497 code_review artifact tickets). For each finding in the dropped pool, read `verification.binary`.\n\nCounts:\n- 145 drops with reason `veto:cited-reference-inaccurate` (other drop reasons: default-advisory 796, low-validity 685, veto:absence-refuted 257, nit-suppressed 252).\n- 10 of the 145 also carry `evidence_entails_finding: \"yes\"`.\n- 5 of those 10 are the parent's shape: the finding reports that the CHANGE under review cites a wrong location or reference, and its own evidence is accurate. Each was re-checked against the reviewed revision fetched from Gerrit:\n  1. Change 1547 PS1 (67b5fa31a23), artifact 5664-f9e6-4cc3-4b08: ADR 0067:38-44 says the cited test pins `drain + cancel`; at that revision the test reads `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS + lock._DEFAULT_TIMEOUT * _DEFAULT_ATTEMPTS` (1200 + 60) and never reads the cancel budget. Finding correct.\n  2. Change 1428 PS1 (9140830d000), artifact 2801-41d0-c6c0-4ba1: ADR 0059:132 cites `capabilities.py:186-206` for `_MODEL_ID_CAPABILITY_OVERRIDES`; the table is at line 317. Finding correct.\n  3. Change 1428 PS2 (fd83b7c863b), artifact 2561-54cc-4600-4eef: same stale anchor, same check. Finding correct.\n  4. Change 2451 PS1 (ed5d973a164), artifact 2752-8c0f-84a8-4cdb: structural-guards.md:119,129 refer to \"Section-1.5\"; Section 1 is a flat list of items 1-5 with no 1.5. Finding correct.\n  5. Change 3056 (155238156af), artifact f018-bef8-ad46-4a80: docs/code-navigation.md cites acli_rest.py:266, dispatch_one.py:321, apply_inbound_events.py:214, binding_store.py:517; at that revision the sites are 292, 400, 269, and none (only a docstring mention at 590). Finding correct.\n- The other 5 eef=yes drops are not about a wrong citation in the change (stale docs for a removed command in 3038; uv image-tag pin; 3 test-coverage findings). Not adjudicated further.\n- A keyword screen of the 135 eef=no drops matched 5 citation-shaped findings; those were not adjudicated, so the 5 above are a floor.\n\nPrior intent: the code-review-verify.md wording dates from 2d3e7611aca (epic b744) and was never revised; doglike-gossipy-pussycat's plan states this ticket applies the same scoping if drops are found. No design fork."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793511096037320001,"uuid":"c2973df5-cf27-410c-88aa-97a873c289c5"}